  "title": "CraftSense",
  "description": "Autocomplete for the crafting table. It tracks what you craft, suggests recipes, and lets you take the result from the output slot without placing the rest of the ingredients!",
  "body": "A Minecraft mod that's like autocomplete for crafting! You don't need to place every ingredient yourself. If it suggests the recipe you want, just take it from the output slot like you normally would (and yes, shift click works too!).\n\nIt also remembers the last item you've crafted, so in that case you don't need to place any ingredients at all! Of course, it only suggests recipes you have the ingredients for.\n\nCategories are generated every time you launch the game, and the mod tracks what you craft in each one. It uses those habits to choose what to suggest, and having many specific categories should make those suggestions pretty (hopefully) helpful.\n\n![CraftSense Showcase](https://cdn.modrinth.com/data/btPzz1Xc/images/20960cbff09dc12fef47bf16fca4b3d9018b3830.png)\n\n## **Usage Guidelines**\n\nCraftSense is only available on Modrinth, CurseForge, and GitHub. Downloads from anywhere else aren't authorized, so please don't use them.",
